We examine the decay width ratios $\Gamma(D	o K\ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(D	o\pi\ell ar{
u})$ and $\Gamma(B	o D\ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(B	o F\ell ar{
u})$ to determine their divergence from the heavy quark limit value of one. Utilizing the light cone sum rules (LCSR) approach, we derive these ratios within the framework of the inverse heavy quark mass expansion. Our findings indicate that the corrections to the infinite mass limit are substantial, reaching approximately 10% for the light quark transitions and 30% for the heavy quark transitions.
